{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhQk3aRxRgYCSd2Hq3MF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression is fixed: a stale worker can no longer change a recovered job or touch the new owner's lock, and the prevalidated suite plus my new tests pass (8 files, 276 tests).\n\n## Cause\n\nThree Redis Lua scripts checked only that a lock *existed*, not that the caller's token *owned* it:\n\n- **`src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`**: the shared helper behind complete, fail, immediate retry, delayed retry, move-to-wait and move-to-waiting-children. It now compares the lock value to the caller's token and returns the existing `-6` (lock mismatch) or `-2` (missing lock) codes.\n- **`src/commands/extendLock-2.lua`**: single-job renewal now requires the token to match, otherwise it returns `0` as before.\n- **`src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua`**: batch renewal now requires a match per job; mismatched or missing jobs come back in the failed-ids list.\n\nEach fix is a one-line change. The ownership check runs before any mutation in each script, so a rejected call leaves state, attempt counters, result, lock and events untouched. The `'0'` token bypass used by administrative APIs is unchanged, and the TypeScript callers needed no change. The PostgreSQL backend already validated tokens; I read it but did not run its tests.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run build` succeeds on Node 24.\n- I added `tests/stale_lock_ownership.redis.test.ts` (8 tests). Each simulates a worker losing its lock, the stalled checker recovering the job, and a second worker claiming it. The tests cover:\n  - stale complete, fail, immediate retry, fixed-backoff delayed retry, and move to delayed/wait: each rejects with `-6` and leaves the job state, job data, lock, events and counts identical;\n  - stale single and batch renewal, which leave the owner's token and TTL alone;\n  - the owner still renewing and finishing its job;\n  - a missing lock still raising `-2`.\n- With the Lua fix stashed, 7 of those 8 fail; the eighth (missing lock) passes either way, as expected.\n\nNo existing tests, package files, build scripts or configuration were edited, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1337,"cache_read_input_tokens":61254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1337},"output_tokens":729,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ca26b3-baa3-428a-8353-3ab78a1aaa81","uuid":"8649ef1d-95ca-4a47-9319-a2da82bb2ac6","timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:10:40.009Z","request_id":"req_011CfhQk2ib8DfqAbo7TtBZT"}
